    "source_record_id": "raw_html_2506296e6d9cb5c5",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\first-year-postpartum-health-and-care-postpartum-sweating_2506296e.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "ee97740fbb5229bf3c7b08799471e522335eb8b1d04a3550e91cb019d0d6ce24"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/postpartum-health-and-care/postpartum-sweating/",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 23,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Postpartum Sweating",
        "text_sha256": "e390cd5c6a0b33af49978ce692613fa52ad8b1d5d1411299cc3fa28f46235fec",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "woman sweating postpartum",
        "text_sha256": "e98d5359618573d5aff7d6c7cd0c2e34e3f733caa82f50aabe81a00e4592fc51",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Plagued with postpartum perspiration? You can chill out — and grab a towel. Here's what to do about that post-baby sweating, especially night sweats after pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "56621f72bb9cf5d951cc9d6b0f81625adfec5f63b0961fcd680fbace1647bf7c",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you find yourself sweating like you've just run a marathon after having a baby, even when you're sitting still, you may be experiencing a very common postpartum symptom: postpartum night sweats.",
        "text_sha256": "b8d8405d4b420e9593ca19eed45230a88df301832337327d815e72c93737e04c",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Postpartum sweating is normal and tends to happen more often when you're sleeping, a phenomenon known as night sweats. Here's everything new moms need to know.",
        "text_sha256": "8d4756c4770887c1ede5ec06426b992834a997b9a0cb634cadeb98aca9191703",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What are postpartum night sweats?",
        "text_sha256": "07789a948f3191bdc9fb66265dd636d70f262392451a4c3396869ca7ea07664f",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Postpartum sweating often happens when you're sleeping and takes the form of postpartum night sweats.",
        "text_sha256": "a56435200bc98b2f14171013ee636684f14964dd0cec8e4eafcf7174dc1b90b0",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Rest assured that even if those damp night sweats are putting a damper on your sleep, lots of perspiration is normal in the weeks after pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "a80d0c24dfcc69759c0e858a8a774da0690c1f22ad9c5a15c5532ba2fd200b1b",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What causes postpartum sweating?",
        "text_sha256": "b83785c030f8e564371c9cd5f688888f5cb4304657270b53b10f8400201a6c89",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your pregnancy hormones are the culprit here again, as they instruct your body to rid itself of all those extra fluids it was formerly using to nourish your baby.",
        "text_sha256": "c0de2935959fb684280fc2bbbe5d2e6bfc36b4abd1189365ebec59f92d6b63a8",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How long do postpartum sweating and postpartum night sweats last?",
        "text_sha256": "38ccb0cef577fdb50091503221c4a79794fcc1660bcd21a374ebe55f514ea9e7",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Postpartum sweating and night sweats will taper off naturally as those extra fluids make their way out and your hormones settle down.",
        "text_sha256": "ff84cc5909a50df220d4bc3e024616356d40fc95e447982f448e307b554b4935",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In the meantime, stay cool and try not to sweat it!",
        "text_sha256": "e62683a6bc8d4033bced3b570be8a79991b580ddc517c1fef248d32efe6773ac",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What can you do about postpartum sweating and postpartum night sweats?",
        "text_sha256": "4c21c30683d1fa0e861ff14314c93623e4f28765cabf1345010cb04fdb0af683",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are several things you can do to make yourself more comfortable if you're sweating a lot after giving birth, whether it's at night, during the day or both.",
        "text_sha256": "48864916181a4d4cbda7d51d0594196c7b4b09a98b64090065d7fcf7681178c9",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "To manage postpartum sweating, try the following:",
        "text_sha256": "b18ef349002a75489abe71ccf25e3c2e662b2ee2e21749d3c1090edce242418d",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Drink up. All that perspiring can leave you dehydrated, so make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids , especially when you first wake up after a bout of night sweats. This is especially important if you're breastfeeding . One easy way to tell if you're getting enough liquids? If your urine is plentiful and a pale yellow color, you're hydrated; if it's dark or scant, you're not.",
        "text_sha256": "c50b39bacd13e1a388ea5b528087919be272acec793715c2b8f39e5613c61e7b",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cover your bedding. Put a soft towel or a pad on your pillow to absorb some of the moisture, and try placing a rubber sheet under your sheets to protect the mattress. This can ease the discomfort of those post-pregnancy night sweats, and save you from washing your bed linens every morning.",
        "text_sha256": "0e3706dfaff25b39f19e463065d11a794b959281dc8eaadd1d0bd36144561c20",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Wear loose, lightweight clothing. Choose cotton, not synthetics — or sleep au naturel.",
        "text_sha256": "4e1a6bc30ca5870c1483bf6dd72df59592f3bdf0fa1fe1a41a1a9f4f3c3a649e",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Crank up the AC or open a window. And tell your partner to grab a sweater or an extra layer if it's cold outside.",
        "text_sha256": "979128d867824fa2e1507667551e126c62d897c2ac8902a9675ac039fd57b1b4",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Sprinkle on some talc-free powder. This'll help to absorb excess moisture and prevent heat rash.",
        "text_sha256": "23d8b70ca74e82057d4575cc938fbd0d65772ab506d19bc47fa7e96fcc3b5079",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you think you might have a fever, take your temperature. If it's over 100.4 degrees Fahrenheit, give your practitioner a call.",
        "text_sha256": "8473edcb36b2d7bfb6ec018e620b0f691746d3ddf35ff493b2c81a0f27b36c38",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just remember that a lot of sweating is normal after you have a baby and it will subside within a few weeks. As always, if you're at all concerned or just need reassurance, give your practitioner a call. In the meantime, do what you can to stay comfortable if you're dealing with postpartum night sweats or the daytime variety.",
        "text_sha256": "2bba17c5bbb735e1c8154cbea2e3fc5ef1e697e28c22370fc887783b48aca0c6",
        "word_count": 59
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 510,
    "heading_count": 5
  },
  "title": "Postpartum Sweating and Postpartum Night Sweats: What's Normal?",
